{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-blueprint/1",
  "name": "Docket Tug",
  "description": "The Traders' tug: a stubby head that does the work and the string it tows. A rubber-fendered push bow, the crew's rooms (bunks, a head, a galley, an airlock over the boarding shaft), engineering behind them and a raised glass wheelhouse over it, glass all round so the pilot watches the tow; four drive nacelles stacked two a side on outriggers. Behind the transom a tow yoke grips the string, an open steel truss three cells long, each taking a standard 2 m container on twist locks on its top for a dock's crane, a railed catwalk down each side to the end car with its legs and tail jets.",
